## kramdown 2.6.0 released

This release brings a minor enhancement and a few bug fixes.

## Changes

* 1 minor change:

  - Enhance header_links option to support specifying content and position (fixes [#831] by Shane
    Becker)

* 9 bug fixes:

  - Fix quadratic-time parsing of unclosed `[` brackets in link/image parser (fixes [#845] by
    Alex J.)
  - Fix 'character class has duplicated range' warning (fixes [#821] by Alexander Popov and [#841]
    by Ryan Davis)
  - Fix crash when a footnote definition has no content (fixes [#829] by Peter Occil with pull
    request [#844) by youdie006)
  - Fix slow parsing of underscores inside words (fixes [#832] by Audrey Hamelers)
  - Fix setting image alt text via IAL on reference style image (fixes [#838] by snan)
  - Emit warning when IAL/ALD contains an invalid (i.e. ignored) part (fixes [#839] by cabo)
  - Fix warning related to deprecated HTMLLegacy formatter of Rouge (fixes [#846] by nicheosala and
    [#842] by Charlotte Van Petegem)
  - Fix parsing of too many nested elements by throwing a `Kramdown::Error`
  - Reduce impact of quadratic time parsing of unclosed HTML comments/instructions/CDATA sections

